Now make the junctions “primes”

Not literal mathematical primes. We deliberately assign primes as unique irreducible labels, essentially a tiny semantic Gödel numbering.

Suppose:

2=\text{difference}

3=\text{relation}

5=\text{flow}

7=\text{boundary}

11=\text{recurrence}

13=\text{transformation}

17=\text{selection}

19=\text{resolution}

A concept can now be represented by a product.

For instance:

\text{wave}=3\cdot5\cdot11=165

because a wave contains relation × flow × recurrence.

A frame might be:

\text{frame}=2\cdot7\cdot17=238

because it creates distinction × boundary × selection.

Music might be:

\text{music}=3\cdot5\cdot11\cdot19=3135

relation, flow, recurrence, resolution.

Now some surprisingly useful mathematics appears.

If

A=3\cdot5\cdot11

and

B=5\cdot7\cdot11

then

\gcd(A,B)=5\cdot11

means their common structural core is:

flow + recurrence.

So GCD becomes abstraction.

Factorization becomes decomposition.

Multiplication becomes composition.

Prime exponent becomes intensity:

2^3 3^1 5^2

could mean unusually strong difference, moderate relation, strong flow.

The representation is no longer merely categorical. It becomes a semantic vector disguised as arithmetic.

